The `ok` in each case only reports key presence, not type. Extensions is map[string]any populated straight from the parsed document (see the UnmarshalJSON implementations that stuff every unknown key into Extensions), so the value type is fully attacker-controlled. The neighbouring code at line 538 shows the correct shape: `if nullable, valid := val.(bool); valid { ... }`.

